"program_narrative": "PORTTEST is a batch test-data program that writes up to WS-MAX-RECORDS (VALUE 100) synthetic portfolio records to the sequential file TEST-FILE, using the PORTFLIO record layout (PORT-RECORD). It takes the current date, opens the file for output and stops at once (close, display, GOBACK) if the open status is not '00'. The main loop builds each record from scratch: a key (PORT-ID from 'PORT' plus the record count; PORT-ACCOUNT-NO from the count plus 1000000000), client information (a name from the prefix 'TEST' plus the count; a one-character client type taken from 'ICT'), portfolio information (create and maintenance dates set to today; a one-character status taken from 'ACS' at a random position) and financial information (a random total value up to 1,000,000 and a cash balance of 10% of it). Each record is written and counted only if the write status is '00'; otherwise an error message is displayed and the loop continues. At the end it closes the file and displays the number of records generated. Error conditions handled: file open failure and write failure (displayed, not counted).",
